  "notes": "USAGE:\n{決断|けつだん} implies a weightier, more consequential decision than {決定|けってい} (which is more neutral and procedural). {決断|けつだん} emphasizes personal resolve and the courage required, while {決定|けってい} focuses on the result of deciding. {判断|はんだん} (judgment) is about evaluating a situation, not necessarily committing to action.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {決断|けつだん}を{下|くだ}す: to make a decision (formal)\n- {決断|けつだん}を{迫|せま}られる: to be pressed for a decision\n- {決断|けつだん}{力|りょく}: decisiveness, decision-making ability\n- {重大|じゅうだい}な{決断|けつだん}: a critical decision\n- {最終|さいしゅう}{決断|けつだん}: final decision",
